        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "And that's now it for this section here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 8.1,
          "en": "Of course, there's way more you could learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.1,
          "end": 12.03,
          "en": "about RxJS and observables and subjects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.03,
          "end": 15,
          "en": "There are many more functions you could learn about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15,
          "end": 19.41,
          "en": "and many more related concepts you could explore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.41,
          "end": 22.86,
          "en": "And you absolutely can consider doing this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.86,
          "end": 25.05,
          "en": "with help of the official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.05,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "and you'll also see some additional examples",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 32.22,
          "en": "throughout the later course sections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.22,
          "end": 36.78,
          "en": "It's just all the worth noting that, as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.78,
          "end": 41.34,
          "en": "RxJS is used in parts of Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 46.32,
          "en": "and is popular in parts of the Angular community,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.32,
          "end": 49.83,
          "en": "and there are teams that heavily use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.83,
          "end": 52.14,
          "en": "But not everyone loves it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.14,
          "end": 54.27,
          "en": "Not everyone wants to work with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.27,
          "end": 56.73,
          "en": "and as an Angular developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 61.38,
          "en": "you don't necessarily need to work with RxJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.38,
          "end": 62.76,
          "en": "especially as of late,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.76,
          "end": 66.87,
          "en": "there also have been some tendencies in the Angular team",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.87,
          "end": 71.87,
          "en": "to make RxJS more optional in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.94,
          "end": 75.81,
          "en": "Either way, you should know what an observable is though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.81,
          "end": 79.86,
          "en": "what its main idea is, what a subject is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.86,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "In the end, an observable where you emit your own values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 87.87,
          "en": "and you should know that you need to subscribe at least once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.87,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "to start it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "and that you can convert from observable to Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 96.15,
          "en": "and vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.15,
          "end": 98.88,
          "en": "And that there are some important differences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.88,
          "end": 102.24000000000001,
          "en": "like that initial value, which a Signal always has,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.24000000000001,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "whereas an observable doesn't necessarily have that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 107.61,
          "en": "And in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.61,
          "end": 110.97,
          "en": "that signals are in the end about managing values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.97,
          "end": 115.44,
          "en": "whereas observables are about managing events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.44,
          "end": 119.91,
          "en": "or values that are emitted by some data source over time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.91,
          "end": 122.673,
          "en": "instead of values that are managed by you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.54,
          "end": 125.85,
          "en": "And of course, it's also worth keeping in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.85,
          "end": 129.24,
          "en": "that you have the massive amount of operators here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.24,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "like that map operator I showed you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 135.27,
          "en": "which can make working with values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.27,
          "end": 138.09,
          "en": "that are produced by an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.09,
          "end": 141.39,
          "en": "easier than it might be with working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.39,
          "end": 143.7,
          "en": "with Signal-based values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.7,
          "end": 146.61,
          "en": "But that, of course, always will depend on your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.61,
          "end": 148.47,
          "en": "and use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.47,
          "end": 150.69,
          "en": "Now you know about both features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.69,
          "end": 152.97,
          "en": "and you'll see both features in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.97,
          "end": 153.803,
          "en": "throughout the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.803,
